            <div xml:id="d879">

                <pb facs="0808" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1160: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-27T10:00:00-06:00">May 27, 1940—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Referring to my dispatch No. 1043, May 23, 1940, I am informed that Honduran
                    Government merely acknowledged memorandum. No further response.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
